  "plain": "In the 1990s, the story goes, a meeting was arranged between one of the heads of EG&G, a defence contractor, and Steven Greer, a campaigner pushing for the government to release what it knows about UFOs, along with a man named Dick D'Amato, and at that meeting UFOs were taken off the table. A researcher who goes by the online name UAPGerb tells Michels this second-hand, citing George Knapp as well as the men involved, among them a man named Alfred O'Donnell. The point of telling it is that people inside the defence world are said to have shut the subject down, and that would mean those insiders had something to protect."
